Windows-only fix in the new native-runner subsystem. canonical_or_original (native.rs) ran the session workspace through Path::canonicalize(), which on Windows returns a \?\ verbatim path; that reached bollard's Mount.source verbatim (manager.rs:294, no normalization) and Docker Desktop rejected it as 'not a valid Windows path'. Root-caused from a live 500 during container create, not tests — Unix canonicalize returns clean paths so CI stayed green and there is no Windows Docker integration test. Fix: strip_verbatim() unwraps only plain drive paths (guards on rest[1]==':'), leaves \?\UNC\ and non-Windows untouched. Considered the dunce crate (purpose-built) but avoided a new dep for a 6-line helper. NOT auto-formatting: workspace_dir on this machine was C:\Users\user\AppData\Local\xpressclaw (desktop app data dir), which is why the mount source pointed there.
